  "notes": "High-risk media policy/runtime behavior change. Source mutation remains forbidden; fallback deletes only the rejected scratch encode temp output after a remux publish succeeds. Representative real-media validation is required before release promotion.\nFallback-remux applies only when post-encode growth exceeds the configured buffer and RouteReasonCode is folder_policy_force_encode.\nFallback remux bypasses direct-copy bitrate caps through the remux fallback entry path, but codec/remux safety policy can still block it; when blocked, the oversized encode is kept with warning evidence.",
